  "result": "I fixed it: `Cart.remove('sku-1')` now removes the Widget line, and all 7 tests pass.\n\n**Root cause:** in `shop/models.py:32`, `Cart.remove` compared the SKU you pass in against the item's **name** instead of its **SKU**:\n\n```python\nself.lines = [l for l in self.lines if l.item.name != sku]\n```\n\n`'Widget' != 'sku-1'` is always true, so no line was ever removed. `Cart.add` already matches on `line.item.sku`, so `remove` didn't match it.\n\n**Fix:** I changed the comparison to `l.item.sku != sku`.\n\n**Checks:**\n- `python3 -m shop.demo` now prints `1`, because only the Gadget line is left.\n- I added a regression test, `tests/test_models.py`, which checks that removing `sku-1` leaves only `sku-2`. It fails on the old code and passes with the fix.\n- pytest isn't installed here, so I ran the tests with `python3 -m unittest`. All 7 pass: the 6 that were already there plus the new one.\n\nI haven't committed anything.",
